The associated time is the light-crossing time: $t_{\mathrm P}
=\frac{\ell_{\mathrm P}}{c}
=\sqrt{\frac{\hbar G}{c^5}}
\approx 5.4\times10^{-44}\,\mathrm s.$ At order-of-magnitude accuracy this is $10^{-43}\,\mathrm s$. It is not an independent construction once the Planck length and the universal speed are known.

